{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBJointAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBJointAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBWP1Capstone","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBEulerTail"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_partB_total_joint_of_no_resonance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_partB_total_joint_of_no_resonance","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBJointAssembly.lean#L71-L103","doc":"**Joint-limit Part-B total (conditional on Diophantine no-resonance).**  Along any filter\n`l` carrying substrate data `q → 1` (`1 < q` eventually), a partition index `n`, and a\nfixed target `0 < x`, with the going-up endpoint reaching the branch point\n(`x·qⁿ → 1⁻`) and the Diophantine no-resonance bound `c·(q−1) ≤ 1 − x·qⁿ` (`c > 0`), the\nPart-B combination\n\n`(q−1)·Σ_{k<n} log(1−x·qᵏ)  −  (1−q⁻¹)·Σ'_{m} (−log(1−q⁻ᵐ⁻¹))  ⟶  Li₂(x) − π²/3`.\n\nThe first summand is the joint W-P1 (positive factors, → `Li₂(x) − π²/6` by\n`tendsto_wp1_sum_of_no_resonance`, #4270); the second is the W-P2 regularized\nnegative-factor Euler tail (→ `π²/6` by `tendsto_wp2_tail_of_q`).  Their difference is the\nPart-B total `Li₂(x) − π²/3` (subtracted just as `naStokes_physical_partB_value` combines\nits two ordered pieces).  This is the **joint** route — the honest genuine limit — gated\nonly on the explicitly-stated no-resonance premise, complementing the iterated (na-Stokes)\nroute which reaches the same value under the ordering conjecture instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_wp2_tail_of_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_wp2_tail_of_q","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBJointAssembly.lean#L50-L69","doc":"**W-P2 Euler-tail along the joint filter.**  The regularized negative-factor tail,\nwritten with the substrate variable `p = 1/q`, converges to `π²/6` along any filter on\nwhich `q → 1` (with `1 < q` eventually).  Immediate from `euler_tail_asymptotic`\n(`Tendsto _ (𝓝[<] 1) (𝓝 π²/6)`) composed with `1/q → 1⁻`: `q → 1` gives `(q)⁻¹ → 1`, and\n`1 < q` gives `(q)⁻¹ < 1`, so `(q)⁻¹ → 1⁻` lands in `𝓝[<] 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}